      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Jonathan Combe from Scotland",
      "description": "The weather was very mixed at Glencoe, where I have returned from a few days holiday. It rained every night but almost every evening brought a great sunset. \nThis was the first night in the area. A visit to the Three sisters, then here, at Glencoe Lochan. \nI arrived at the Lochan to be greeted with perfect reflections and a great sky, too. The problem with these locations at this time of year are midges. There was a countless number at this spot alone and have actually had to clone some out as they were stuck to the filters.. \nAll in all it was a good holiday and I have a few more shots to post. \n\nThanks for looking.",
      "dateCreated": "2013-07-27 20:50",
